.SH DEBUG OUTPUT
You can add \f[CR]\-\-debug[=N]\f[R] to the command line to log debug
output.
N ranges from 1 (least output, the default) to 9 (maximum output).
Typically you would start with 1 and increase until you are seeing
enough.
Debug output goes to stderr, interleaved with the requests logged on
stdout.
To capture debug output in a log file instead, you can usually redirect
stderr, eg:
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[CR]hledger\-web \-\-debug=3 2>hledger\-web.log\f[R].
.SH LANGUAGE
hledger\-web\(aqs pages can be shown in another language when a
translation catalog is available (see Languages in the hledger manual).
.PP
When hledger\-web is started with \f[CR]\-\-lang LANG\f[R], eg
\f[CR]\-\-lang de\f[R], every page is in that language, whatever the
browser asks for.
So you can use hledger\-web in a language other than your browser\(aqs,
or give every user of a shared server the same language.
.PP
Otherwise the language is chosen per request, and the first of these
naming an available translation wins:
.IP "1." 3
a \f[CR]_LANG\f[R] query parameter, eg \f[CR]?_LANG=de\f[R].
This choice is remembered in a \f[CR]_LANG\f[R] cookie.
.IP "2." 3
the \f[CR]_LANG\f[R] cookie
.IP "3." 3
the browser\(aqs \f[CR]Accept\-Language\f[R] header, ie the browser\(aqs
or system\(aqs language settings
.PP
If none does, pages are in English, or with \f[CR]\-\-lang auto\f[R], in
the language of hledger\-web\(aqs environment.
So viewers usually get their browser\(aqs language automatically, if
hledger\-web has it.
Catalogs, including any in the config directory, are loaded when
hledger\-web starts.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\f[B]LEDGER_FILE\f[R] The main journal file to use when not specified
with \f[CR]\-f/\-\-file\f[R].
Default: \f[CR]$HOME/.hledger.journal\f[R].
